    "title": "A=1 shape-A three-class Koszul/Gram router",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "exact three-quadratic generation and proportional classwise source Gram matrices",
    "statement": "Let V be the parameter coefficient space of the Shape-A split biform G and r=dim V. Each of the three source classes has n+2 or n+3 domain points, so each class alone spans V. If q_alpha=ell_beta ell_theta and cyclically, then P_e=q_alpha V+q_beta V+q_theta V and the restricted Koszul map V^3->P_e is surjective with kernel dimension 3r-(e+1). For J={h:ell_alpha h,ell_beta h,ell_theta h in V}, the triple shifted intersection is ell_alpha ell_beta ell_theta J and 2dim J<=3r-(e+1). The two endpoint source-frame cancellations make the three classwise weighted locator Gram matrices proportional to one symmetric K, with im K in the triple intersection and max(0,2r-(n+2))<=rank K<=dim J. Officially the minimum live rank has Koszul kernel dimension two, and K is forced nonzero once r>=137438953472.",
